1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,304
Here is why position matters.

2
00:00:02,304 --> 00:00:11,757
When hydroxide adds to the carbon carrying chlorine, the ring briefly holds an extra negative charge, before chloride leaves.

3
00:00:11,757 --> 00:00:18,398
That charge moves around the ring, landing on the carbons ortho and para to the point of attack.

4
00:00:18,398 --> 00:00:28,632
With a nitro group para, the charge reaches the nitro carbon and spreads onto its oxygens, so the intermediate is stabilised and the reaction is fast.

